Package: pSI
Type: Package
Title: Specificity Index Statistic
Version: 1.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Xiaoxiao", "Xu", role = "aut"),
    person("Alan B.", "Wells", role = "aut"),
    person("David R.", "O'Brien", email = "dunder.chief@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0007-0339-0517")),
    person("Arye", "Nehorai", role = "aut"),
    person("Joseph D.", "Dougherty", role = "aut"))
Description: Calculates the Specificity Index (pSI) statistic, which identifies
    genes enriched in specific cell types or tissues from a matrix of expression
    profiles, and provides post-processing tools: lists and counts of specific
    genes at standard pSI thresholds, overlap with candidate gene lists, and
    Fisher's exact tests for enrichment of a candidate gene list across all cell
    types and thresholds (Cell type-Specific Expression Analysis, CSEA). The
    methods are described in Dougherty et al. (2010) <doi:10.1093/nar/gkq130>,
    Xu et al. (2014) <doi:10.1523/JNEUROSCI.4488-13.2014> and Wells et al.
    (2015) <doi:10.1093/nar/gkv1262>. The precomputed pSI tables for mouse cell
    types and human brain regions used in those papers, formerly the 'pSI.data'
    package, are downloaded on first use with psi_data().
